{
  "id": "V20",
  "title": "Strong-Wall WSWH on concrete with a sheathed wall",
  "intent": "A WSWH18 panel on a concrete foundation (9 ft story, exact WSWH18x9 row) shares the story shear with an 8 ft sheathed wall by capacity: the panel weight is its tabulated V_allow (lb), the wall weight is v_cap × L. Checks the vertical load P used for the table lookup, the panel D/C = V_ASD / V_allow, the anchor tension T = 0.7V·H_e/B − (0.6−0.14S_DS)·P/2, the Table 06 anchor (cracked concrete, SDC D → seismic \"E\" rows only, smallest W then d_e), and the panel drift Δ = Δ_cap·V/V_cap.",
  "covers": [
    "Simpson C-L-SW26 Table 01 (WSWH18x9)",
    "Table 05 arm B",
    "Table 06-A anchors (cracked, 2,500 psi)",
    "Capacity distribution with WSWH"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Panel SW-1 WSWH18 (1.5 ft wide), no wall weight; point load D = 1.2 k on the panel. P (ASD, seismic) = max[(1.0 + 0.14S_DS)D, (1.0 + 0.105S_DS)D + 0.75L] = 1.14 × 1200 = 1368 lb."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "Table 01, WSWH18x9 (nominal 9 ft = floor-to-floor, f'c 2,500 psi): H_e = 105.25 in; P = 1,000 and 4,000 lb rows both give V_ASD,S = 2,575 lb and Δ = 0.45 in → at P = 1368 lb: V_allow = 2,575 lb. Arm B = 12.5 in (Table 05)."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "Capacity distribution, SW-2 at 6\" o.c. (312 plf): weights panel 2,575 lb, SW-2 312 × 8 = 2496 lb → Σ = 5071 lb. Panel V = 4 × 2575/5071 = 2.031 k; SW-2 V = 1.969 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "SW-2: v = 0.7 × 1.969 × 1000/8 = 172.27 plf ≤ 312 → 6\" o.c. (unchanged, so the weights hold). N = 1.969 × 9/8 = 2.215 k, T = 0.7 × 2.215 − 0.46 × 0.36 = 1.385 k → HDUE3."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "Panel D/C = V_ASD / V_allow = 0.7 × 2.031 × 1000 / 2575 = 1422 / 2575 = 0.552."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "Panel anchor tension, (0.6 − 0.14S_DS)D + 0.7E: T = 0.7·V·H_e/B − 0.46·D/2 = 0.7 × 2.031 × 105.25/12.5 − 0.46 × 0.60 = 11.696 k = 11696 lb."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "Table 06-A (2,500 psi, cracked), SDC D → criteria E only. Rows with T_ASDallow ≥ 11696 lb, smallest W then d_e: STD 16,000 lb, W = 33 in, d_e = 11 in (L_ftg = 47 in for WSWH18) → WSWH-AB STD (E), D/C = 0.731."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Panel drift at 1.0E: Δ = Δ_LRFD·V/V_LRFD = 0.64 × 2031.16 / 3680 = 0.353 in (linear from the LRFD cap with its drift; V ≤ V_LRFD → no warning)."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "Line checks G1–G12 pass (the panel load goes straight to the foundation)."
    },
    {
      "step": 10,
      "text": "Story drift inputs: SW-1 (WSWH) δ = the table drift of step 8 (LRFD seismic column Δ_LRFD = 0.64 in at V_LRFD = 3,680 lb, scaled to the 1.0E share 2031.16 lb) = 0.353 in. SW-2 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 1.969 / 8 = 246.11 plf, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 16 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0101; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.1384; uplift end T = 2214.95 lb (lateral); Δ_HD = δ_LRFD × T / T_LRFD = 0.178 × 2214.95 / 5306 = 0.0743 (HDUE3); r = 2214.95 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.3375 → Δ_c = 0.0092; h·Δa/b = 9 × (0.0743 + 0.0092) / 8 = 0.0940 → δ = 0.2425 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 11,
      "text": "Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-1 0.3532 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.3532 / 1.0 = 1.413 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 9 × 12 = 2.160 in → OK."
    }
  ],
